To incorporate the APPE (Append) and DELE (Delete) client requests into the existing sequence, we can place the APPE request after the LIST command (assuming you want to append data after listing the files), and the DELE request can be placed before QUIT (assuming you want to delete a file before quitting). 

Here’s the modified sequence of client requests:

```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
LIST
APPE filename_to_append
DELE filename_to_delete
QUIT
```

In this sequence, replace `filename_to_append` and `filename_to_delete` with the actual names of the files you want to append to and delete, respectively

